---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@data/site";
import { leadershipNetwork, leadershipResponsibilities, organisation } from "@data/research";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Leadership"
  description="SCSDA is led by its Founding Dean, Dr Daguang Han, who chairs the Governing Committee. This page sets out the leadership, the centre structure and the collaboration around it."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Leadership</p>
        <h2>Founding Dean and Chair of the Governing Committee.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section-copy">
        <p>
          Dr Daguang Han founded the Academy in April 2019 and leads it as
          Dean, now in his second term. He chairs the Governing Committee, the
          Academy's governing board, and is its legal representative. The
          Liangjiang New Area government approval of March 2019 names him as
          the Academy's designated head. As Dean he holds delegated authority
          for recruitment, contracting and budget.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Academy today has a core team of 14 and twelve jointly
          established research centres and laboratories, four of them with
          European partner universities. A visiting professorship network of
          seventeen senior experts is engaged under institutional agreements,
          sixteen of them professors. Thirteen incubation projects have come
          out of the research, and three companies have been registered. The
          Academy has passed the government's annual review every year since
          it was founded.
        </p>
        <p>
          Leadership here is an institutional function: setting research
          directions, running the centre structure, coordinating expert
          participation, developing partner-facing projects, and reporting
          applied research outputs through public channels. Expert advisers,
          centre-level academic and technical leads, project collaborators and
          enterprise partners work within that structure across SCSDA's smart
          city, digital construction, sensing, and sustainable development
          agenda.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Academy's cross-border work has also been carried at governance
          level rather than only at project level: from 2021 to 2022 Dr Han
          served as Vice-President of the International Center for Innovation
          Cooperation (ICIC). That vantage informs how SCSDA structures its own partnerships &mdash;
          every joint centre rests on a dated signed agreement, because an
          arrangement that has to survive staff changes on both sides cannot
          rest on personal contact alone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dr Han's current work carries the Academy's digital construction and
          sensing agenda forward: reality capture and point clouds turned into
          models that can be checked, automated checking of design rules, and
          condition assessment of ageing steel structures. He is Lead Guest
          Editor of a Future Cities (Emerald) special issue on renewing ageing
          infrastructure, and a member of ASCE and IEEE.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell highlight-grid">
      <article class="case-card">
        <img
          src="/images/sensor-calibration-equipment.jpg"
          alt="Precision sensor development and calibration equipment in an Academy laboratory"
          width="1080"
          height="720"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div class="case-body">
          <span class="category">Working style</span>
          <h3>Leadership close to the laboratory</h3>
          <p>Platform leadership at SCSDA stays close to the technical work: reviewing experimental setups and instrumentation, and connecting research groups with the questions their methods can answer.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Organisation Structure</p>
        <h2>Governing Committee, Dean, deputy deans, research units and functional centres.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Governing Committee is the Academy's governing board and is
        chaired by the Dean. Two committees advise it. Three deputy deans
        report to the Dean, and the work is carried out in nine research units
        and six functional centres.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell org-chart" role="group" aria-label="Organisation structure of the Academy">
      <div class="org-row org-row-three">
        <div class="org-box org-advisory">
          <h3>{organisation.advisory[0].title}</h3>
          <p>{organisation.advisory[0].text}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="org-box">
          <h3>{organisation.governing.title}</h3>
          <p>{organisation.governing.text}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="org-box org-advisory">
          <h3>{organisation.advisory[1].title}</h3>
          <p>{organisation.advisory[1].text}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="org-link" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="org-row org-row-dean">
        <div class="org-box org-lead">
          <h3>{organisation.dean.title}</h3>
          <p>{organisation.dean.text}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="org-box org-advisory">
          <h3>{organisation.honorary.title}</h3>
          <p>{organisation.honorary.text}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="org-link" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="org-row org-row-three">
        {organisation.deputies.map((item) => (
          <div class="org-box">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="org-link" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="org-row org-row-three">
        {organisation.units.map((unit) => (
          <div class="org-box org-unit">
            <h3>{unit.title}</h3>
            <p class="org-lead-line">{unit.lead}</p>
            <ul class="clean-list">
              {unit.items.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="org-note">
        Solid outline: line responsibility. Dashed outline: advisory. Research
        units are shown as organised today. The April 2023 acceptance report
        counted twelve research centres and laboratories established with
        partners, four of them with European partner universities; they are
        listed on the <a href="/research/">Research</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell theme-grid">
      {leadershipNetwork.map((item) => (
        <article class="theme-card">
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Leadership Scope</p>
        <h2>Strategic, academic, and industry-facing responsibilities.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Leading the Academy is platform-building work: agenda setting, centre
        formation, partner development, project formation, expert engagement,
        institutional reporting, and public communication. These
        responsibilities turn a technical strategy into centres, projects,
        people, partnerships, and outputs that academic and industry audiences
        can review.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell theme-grid">
      {leadershipResponsibilities.map((item) => (
        <article class="theme-card">
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell article narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">External References</p>
      <h2>Selected public reference links.</h2>
      <p>
        Selected public reference links are provided only for source
        transparency where the Academy's leadership is discussed.
      </p>
      <div class="profile-links">
        {site.profiles.map((profile) => (
          <a href={profile.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{profile.label}</a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
